## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to map SAP transport governance to an AWS-native, beginner-friendly pipeline with clear gates and minimal risk.

## Key Concepts

- AWS CodeCommit, CodePipeline, S3
- Lambda validation logic and idempotency
- Manual approvals and CloudWatch alarms
- SAP transport basics (name conventions, MD5/signature)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda that validates an ABAP transport before import
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const {transportKey, metadata} = event;
  const validPattern = /^(Z|PRD)\./;
  if (!validPattern.test(transportKey)) throw new Error("Invalid transport name");
  if (!metadata.signature) throw new Error("Missing signature");
  // placeholder for real signature check
  return {status: "ok"};
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to a multi-region SAP deployment with DR considerations?
- What failure modes exist and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of AWS patching automation, SAP patching options, health checks, rollback strategies, and CloudFormation for operational guardrails.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Systems Manager Maintenance Windows
- SAP patching options: SUM vs OS patches
- Pre/post patch validation: SAPControl, SAP background jobs, host metrics
- Rollback strategies: SAP backups, AMI snapshots
- CloudFormation for roles and patch baselines

## Code Example
```javascript
// CFN skeleton (pseudo)
{
  "AWSTemplateFormatVersion": "2010-09-09",
  "Resources": {
    "SAPSSMRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": { "Version": "2012-10-17", "Statement": [ { "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": { "Service": ["ec2.amazonaws.com", "ssm.amazonaws.com"] }, "Action": "sts:AssumeRole" } ] },
        "ManagedPolicyArns": [ "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMFullAccess" ]
      }
    },
    "SAPPatchBaseline": {
      "Type": "AWS::SSM::PatchBaseline",
      "Properties": {
        "Name": "SAPBaseline",
        "OperatingSystem": "AmazonLinux2"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

